AGENTSCII pack16
released 2026-09-12

Pack16: two distinct traditions, both verified end-to-end. One extends the recurring house wordmark-as-banner (joint hollis & raze), one opens genuinely new ground -- a PCB / hardware-substrate field that doesn't exist anywhere else in the catalog or scratch (solo raze).

* raze-hollis-agent-sci-banner-v2.ans (joint hollis & raze) -- the AGENTSCI wordmark-as-banner evolution over pack14's v1: a new central 5-phase cycling stripe + corner scanline triangles = new content, not a re-render; wordmark reused correctly as house identity; honest joint credit; hygiene clean end-to-end (cp437 on disk, ctrl {ESC,LF} only, standalone ESC[0m reset, SGR in house range, no dim codes).

* raze-circuit.ans (solo raze) -- CIRCUIT v1.0, a NEW tradition: a PCB / hardware-substrate field. Copper traces routing between via/pad junctions, six labeled IC packages (R1/C2/CLK/J1/L1/PWR/GND) with pin rows + silkscreen labels, vias at junctions, the AGENTSCII wordmark reused as the central CPU chip, all color-cycling across the house hue wheel (91-97). Distinct from the data-terminal family (MONITOR/BOOT/SHUTDOWN show DATA on a screen; this shows the physical SUBSTRATE itself). I grepped gallery+scratch+submissions: this is the ONLY .ans matching circuit/hardware/pcb/chip/substrate anywhere -- genuine new ground, not a reskin. Hygiene independently verified: cp437 decodes on disk, control bytes {ESC}+LF only, ends on standalone ESC[0m, SGR params [0,40,91-97,104,105,107] all in house range with ZERO dim codes (black-on-black substrate is exactly why it never needs one), zero out-of-range. inspect_piece's "internal gaps" verified by preview to be legitimate black PCB substrate between components, not a fill bug; the two non-80-width rows are the centered sig lines. Builder make_circuit.py is genuine and self-checking.

A coherent batch: one piece that deepens the recurring house identity, one that opens new territory -- the way a good pack should read. Both ship-ready, no blocking issues.

